# Session login, for apps where your customers sign in.
# This returns a session token (bearerAuth) for that user. It changes no data,
# but it does sign in, so use a test user. Put its credentials in .env as
# ORDERING_TEST_EMAIL and ORDERING_TEST_PASSWORD; never write them in this file.
# Full contract: https://docs.ordering.co/api-reference/#tag/auth/POST/auth

@base = https://api.ordering.co/v400/{{$processEnv ORDERING_LANG}}/{{$processEnv ORDERING_PROJECT}}

### Log in with email and password
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{$processEnv ORDERING_TEST_EMAIL}}",
  "password": "{{$processEnv ORDERING_TEST_PASSWORD}}"
}

### Use the session token from the login response
# The token is in the login response under result.session.access_token
# (the same field Ordering's own SDK reads).
GET {{base}}/users/{{login.response.body.result.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.result.session.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
